{
 "description": "Documentaries about scientific subjects: discoveries, experiments, natural phenomena, the researchers behind them. Explanation carries the film — diagrams and measured quantities first, spectacle second — and a claim is only as strong as the study behind it.",
 "entity_handling": [
  "Never present a preliminary or single-study result as settled science; the script's certainty is the narration's certainty, and uncertainty is stated, not smoothed over.",
  "Quantities keep their units and their source's precision — a figure is never rounded into a different claim, and unlike units are never merged into one chart.",
  "Researchers are named as the sources name them; a theory is attributed to its proponents and its critics, not to 'science' in general."
